  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-20T16:12:25.077Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi everyone\nI noticed after VRCHAT 2021.2.2 update, the vram leaks render the game pretty much unplayable (mid 20fps in PyPyDance with under 10 avatars), also a lot higher vram usage in other world as well.\n\nIn PyPyDance, the vram usage is up to 9.8Gb with CPU frametime at 45-55ms, GPU frametime at 20-25ms.\nI tried to reinstall the game and reinstall GPU driver, unfortunately result in no improvement. \nOther than OVR in the background, there is nothing else running in the background. SteamVR SS tested at 50% to 150%, fps/frametime/vram usage stay the same.\n\nAny help would be appreciated. Thank you\nPC specs:\nCPU: AMD Ryzen 7 5800x\nGPU: NVIDIA RTX3080\nRAM: 32Gb (at least 20Gb free at all time).\nHMD: HTC Vive Pro",
